The last code changes were to `buildFloor()` and `buildWalls()` to implement intelligent auto-alignment with proper Y=0 positioning where floor top surface = Y=0 and walls sit on that surface.

Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

**Main Goal:** Fix NajikaCore 3D scene where previous AI damaged the code, causing:
- Skeleton Mage character positioning issues (head stuck in ground or body floating)
- Floor/wall misalignment issues
- KayKit 3D assets not loading (showing fallback grid room instead)

**Specific User Requirements:**
- Skeleton should stand correctly on the ground with feet at Y=0
- Floor should be thin/flat, not thick
- Floor should align perfectly with walls (no gaps, no overlap)
- Walls should be positioned at the edge of the floor, not in the middle
- Implement auto-alignment system similar to old script that adjusted everything when room size changed
- All 3D models (KayKit assets) should load with textures, not fallback grid

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- **Three.js 3D Scene Management**: Camera modes (Orbit, Third-person, First-person), lighting, shadows
- **GLTF Model Loading**: GLTFLoader for KayKit asset packs (furniture, dungeons, skeletons)
- **Bounding Box Calculations**: `THREE.Box3().setFromObject()` for ground positioning
- **Lazy Loading Pattern**: Loading room assets on-demand when switching rooms
- **Y-Axis Ground Alignment**: Critical concept that Y=0 represents the floor surface
- **Asset Positioning Strategy**: 
  - Floor: Top surface at Y=0, bottom extends below
  - Walls: Bottom edge at Y=0, extending upward
  - Characters/Props: Bottom/feet at Y=0
- **Event-Driven Architecture**: `kaykit:modelLoaded` and `kaykit:configReady` events
- **Scale Transformations**: Uniform scaling for floor, axis-specific for walls

## 3. Files and Code Sections

### **C:\NajikaCore\digivice\js\3d_scene.js** (Main changes)

**Purpose:** Core Three.js scene manager handling room building, character positioning, and 3D rendering

**Key Function: `adjustToGround()` - CRITICAL FIX** (Lines 597-601)
```javascript
function adjustToGround(group) {
    const box = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(group);
    const offsetY = box.min.y;
    group.position.y -= offsetY;
}
```
**Why this matters:** Previous version manipulated child positions causing skeleton head to be buried. New version moves the entire group, keeping internal structure intact.

**Function: `buildFloor()` - FINAL AUTO-ALIGNMENT** (Lines 469-483)
```javascript
function buildFloor(entry, span) {
    const instance = makeModelInstance(entry);
    if (!instance) return null;
    // Skaliere Boden auf volle span-Größe
    scaleUniformToSpan(instance, span);
    // Mache Boden EXTREM flach (nur 5% Höhe) wie eine dünne Platte
    instance.scale.y *= 0.05;
    // Berechne BoundingBox um Boden korrekt zu positionieren
    const box = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(instance);
    const floorHeight = box.max.y - box.min.y;
    // Positioniere so dass OBERSEITE bei Y=0 ist (Unterseite darunter)
    instance.position.y = -box.min.y - floorHeight;
    applyEntryTransform(instance, entry);
    return instance;
}
```
**Why this matters:** Ensures floor top surface is exactly at Y=0, matching where character feet should be. The 5% height makes it thin like a plate.

**Function: `buildWalls()` - AUTO-ALIGNMENT SYSTEM** (Lines 485-533)
```javascript
function buildWalls(entry, span, wallHeight) {
    const base = makeModelInstance(entry);
    if (!base) return null;

    // Skaliere Wand-Modell auf die volle span-Breite
    scaleAxisToSpan(base, 'x', span);

    const group = new THREE.Group();
    // Wände am RAND des Bodens positionieren (span / 2)
    const half = span / 2;

    const north = cloneGroup(base);
    north.position.set(0, 0, -half);
    group.add(north);

    const south = cloneGroup(base);
    south.rotation.y = Math.PI;
    south.position.set(0, 0, half);
    group.add(south);

    const east = cloneGroup(base);
    east.rotation.y = -Math.PI / 2;
    east.position.set(half, 0, 0);
    group.add(east);

    const west = cloneGroup(base);
    west.rotation.y = Math.PI / 2;
    west.position.set(-half, 0, 0);
    group.add(west);

    group.traverse(node => {
        if (node.isMesh) {
            node.castShadow = true;
            node.receiveShadow = true;
        }
    });

    // Skaliere Wand-Höhe auf gewünschte wallHeight
    const currentHeight = getBoundingSize(group).y;
    const scaleFactor = wallHeight / Math.max(currentHeight, 0.0001);
    group.scale.y *= scaleFactor;

    // WICHTIG: Wände mit UNTERSEITE auf Y=0 (Boden-Oberseite)
    const box = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(group);
    group.position.y = -box.min.y;

    applyEntryTransform(group, entry);
    return group;
}
```
**Why this matters:** Implements the auto-alignment system user requested. Walls automatically position at floor edges (span/2) and sit on ground (Y=0), adjusting when room size changes.

**Function: `applyEntryTransform()` - BUG FIX** (Lines 618-648)
```javascript
function applyEntryTransform(group, entry) {
    if (!entry) return;

    if (typeof entry.scale === 'number') {
        group.scale.multiplyScalar(entry.scale);
    } else if (Array.isArray(entry.scale)) {
        const [sx = 1, sy = 1, sz = 1] = entry.scale;
        group.scale.x *= sx;
        group.scale.y *= sy;
        group.scale.z *= sz;
    }

    if (Array.isArray(entry.rotation)) {
        const [rx = 0, ry = 0, rz = 0] = entry.rotation;
        group.rotation.set(rx, ry, rz);
    }

    if (Array.isArray(entry.position)) {
        const [px = 0, py = 0, pz = 0] = entry.position;
        // Nur X und Z setzen, Y wird durch adjustToGround() bestimmt
        group.position.x += px;
        group.position.z += pz;
        // Y-Offset wird NACH adjustToGround angewendet
        if (py !== 0) {
            group.position.y += py;
        }
    }

    // adjustToGround wurde bereits vorher aufgerufen, nicht nochmal!
    // adjustToGround(group);
}
```
**Why this matters:** Removed duplicate `adjustToGround()` call that was causing props and characters to be positioned twice, burying them underground.

**Function: `changeRoom()` - ASSET LOADING FIX** (Lines 902-910)
```javascript
changeRoom(name) {
    if (name) {
        currentRoomName = name;
        if (window.KayKitLoader && typeof KayKitLoader.loadRoomOnDemand === 'function') {
            KayKitLoader.loadRoomOnDemand(name);
        }
        scheduleRoomBuild();
    }
}
```
**Why this matters:** Without this, KayKit assets weren't loading when switching rooms, causing fallback grid room to display.

**Function: `loadCharacter()` - SKELETON POSITIONING** (Lines 696-726)
```javascript
function loadCharacter() {
    if (!THREE.GLTFLoader) {
        console.warn('Scene3D: GLTFLoader missing; cannot load Skeleton_Mage.');
        return;
